WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.060
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.070
happening all the time, so we gathered

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.090
some of the most-hyped
products from October

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.600
to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.040
Let's start off with these new products

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.760
from Huda Beauty's GloWish line,

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.101
the Luminous Pressed Powder

00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:13.534
and the Cheeky Vegan Blush.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.060
I have yet to be disappointed
by a GloWish product,

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.130
but this powder wasn't my favorite.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.782
It is super silky and
soft, but I felt like

00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:22.720
because it's a luminous pressed powder,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.370
on my bare skin, it
just highlighted texture

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:26.920
in a way I didn't love.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.450
I had a feeling I would like
this more over foundation --

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.560
you can use it both ways --

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.100
so I tried it that way, and, yep,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.920
I feel like it looks
smoother over the foundation

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.510
than just on my bare skin.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.880
And the blush was cute,

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.280
nothing really special.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.070
I don't think it's worth paying $21

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.890
for a just-OK blush,

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.740
especially one that's so baby-sized.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.060
This water-activated
liner from Matte Lashes

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.750
is supposed to be super
pigmented and transfer-proof,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.460
so I was dying to try it out.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.830
All you do with these is
dip your brush in some water

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.120
and wet the liner.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.850
I put some on the back of my hand first

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.980
just to see how
transfer-proof it actually is,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.490
and it did not move.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.800
It also dried down super
matte, which I love.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.240
I hate when black liner has
that shiny satin finish.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.080
Applying it on the eyes was so easy.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.470
I actually prefer using
these kinds of liners,

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.510
because I feel like

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.690
I just have more control of the product.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.480
I can see myself using this all the time,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.629
and it actually comes in a set

00:01:17.629 --> 00:01:19.130
with a white liner too.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.888
This is a product that I don't think

00:01:20.888 --> 00:01:21.988
I ever would have tried

00:01:21.988 --> 00:01:23.490
if it wasn't for this show.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.873
This is the Makeup by Mario

00:01:24.873 --> 00:01:26.764
Master Metals Eyeshadow Palette,

00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:29.900
and it has all these really
beautiful metallic shades

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.040
that can be used wet or dry.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.560
I used this orange copper shade dry first,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.860
just applying it straight
on the eye with my finger,

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.930
and these are so smooth and metallic.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.730
They really do make your eyes pop.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.330
Then I scraped up some powder

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.400
to mix together with the Metal Manipulator

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.470
to basically turn it into a liquid.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.150
This is sold separately, by the way.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.570
Using these in the liquid form

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.660
intensifies it by, like, 1,000.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.200
It literally looks like
liquid metal on the eyes.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.390
And the Metal Manipulator
makes it budge-proof,

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.970
so it won't smudge anywhere.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.863
I'm still not super into the idea

00:02:01.863 --> 00:02:04.920
of a $48 all-metallic palette,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.780
but the quality of these
shadows is so, so good.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:08.830
Next, let's talk about

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.330
the Milani Color Fetish Matte Lipsticks.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.900
Oh, my God, I think I love these.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.600
They are incredibly creamy,
smooth, and pigmented.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.620
I love the soft matte finish they have.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.623
Everything about these

00:02:19.623 --> 00:02:22.310
feels more expensive
than they actually are.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.610
They are so cute.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.960
Definitely recommend these.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.140
This color, Secret, in particular

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.040
is supposed to be a Charlotte
Tilbury Pillow Talk dupe.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.100
I can't speak on that

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.820
because I don't have Pillow Talk money,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.220
but I'm just letting you know.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.050
And, finally, we have the
Em Cosmetics So Soft sticks.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.820
I have the Multi Faceplay stick,

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.720
which can be used as bronzer or contour,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.000
and the blush stick.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.910
The name does not lie.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.550
These are some of the softest,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.350
most easy-to-blend
products I've ever used.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.620
I don't normally contour,

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.730
but this color was more on the cool side,

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.650
so I attempted to contour with it,

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.620
and it was just so easy
to apply and blend.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:02:59.720
Same with the blush.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.800
The color was a little too light for me,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.400
but because they blend in so easy,

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.770
I think I made it work.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.100
These are pricey,

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.588
but so worth it to me.

